  <bounds minlat="41.392250" minlon="2.173700" maxlat="41.397150" maxlon="2.180100"/>

  <!--
    4×4 grid of signalised intersections (~150 m spacing), 3 lanes per
    direction. Derived from test_4x4.osm's layout, but each physical
    street is ONE bidirectional way (lanes=6, turn:lanes:forward/
    turn:lanes:backward = left|through|right) instead of two coincident
    oneway ways — netconvert only spreads opposite-direction lanes
    apart from a single tagged bidirectional way; two independently
    authored oneway ways sharing endpoints collapse onto the same
    physical lanes once lane count > 1.

    All <node> elements are declared before any <way>: netconvert's OSM
    reader silently drops a way whose node(s) appear later in the
    document, so nodes and ways cannot be interleaved per-street.

    Intersection nodes C[row,col] use ids 5001-5016 (row-major, row 1 = bottom).
    Each node carries highway=traffic_signals so SUMO treats it as a junction.

    col:   1         2         3         4
    row 4: 5013 == 5014 == 5015 == 5016
           |         |         |         |
    row 3: 5009 == 5010 == 5011 == 5012
           |         |         |         |
    row 2: 5005 == 5006 == 5007 == 5008
           |         |         |         |
    row 1: 5001 == 5002 == 5003 == 5004

    Row ways (1XX) digitized west->east = forward; column ways (3XX)
    digitized south->north = forward. netconvert derives the opposite
    direction as edge "-1XX"/"-3XX". External terminal stubs (9XX) let
    vehicles enter/leave off the grid, forward = entering the grid.
  -->

